course: dictionary
lesson: 8614
title: Screech: a loud, harsh sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. Say «screech» aloud and you can almost hear a high, harsh, scary noise. Read the words around it to check. «Tasmanian devils screech and growl to sort out who eats first» tells you the sound is part of a noisy, angry fight.
explain: «Once a tyre slides, it grips less than when it rolls, which is why a spinning tyre screeches.» The clue is grips less: the tyre is losing its hold on the road, so it makes a sharp, scraping noise. The sentence gives you a reason for the sound.
explain: Screech can also mean to stop very suddenly, as in «screech to a halt». Try the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence. «The car stopped suddenly with a loud, harsh noise» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Screech can be a verb (to screech) or a noun (a screech).
fact: To screech is to make a very loud, high, harsh sound.
fact: «Screech to a halt» means to stop very suddenly, often with a screeching noise.
fact: When brakes screech, the car is stopping hard, so screeching brakes are a warning on the road.
fact: A barn owl is called a screech owl in some places.
exercise: «A spinning tyre screeches on the road.» What is the tyre making? | A sweet smell | A quiet hum | *A sharp, scraping noise | A bright light
exercise: The car had to screech to a halt. What does that mean? | Turn around and go back | *Stop very suddenly | Drive very slowly for a long time | Park neatly in a space
exercise: In «The owl gave a loud screech», what kind of word is screech? | A full stop | An adjective | A verb | *A noun
test: Why is a spinning tyre said to screech? | It is singing a song | *It is sliding and gripping less, so it makes a harsh scraping sound | It is dry and cold | It is very new and shiny
test: «In the 1990s many homes used dial-up modems, which screeched as they connected.» What does this tell you about them? | They were quick and quiet | They played music | *They made a loud, harsh noise and were slow | They were made of wood
exam: Which word fits best in «The brakes ___ as the bus stopped suddenly.»? | whispered | painted | *screeched | slept
